// Ch6 B05 "The barge leaves no wake": Sefir's first appearance (act1_ch06.md B05; ADR 0017 (a),
// ADR 0020 (i), ADR 0022 (f)). Letterboxed. W10 → W11 → W10 → W12 → W13 → W12 → W10.
// The staging contract, in order (every numbered block below is one item of the sheet):
//   1 the impasse; 2 the barge leaves no wake; 3 Kerrid's back; 4 the one sentence; 5 the rebuke and
//   the question he declines; 6 "I knelt beside your mother"; 7 Liss on Toma's papers, and the crate;
//   8 Ysolde; 9 Rhen, a likeable boy; 10 Toma overjoyed; 11 the going.
// Rules (tests/integration/test_ch06_thread.gd checks the ones a test can):
//   - Sefir's lines are the sheet's, verbatim. He never raises his voice, never hurries, never uses a
//     contraction. He answers no grief here.
//   - He stays aboard at the bow for the whole scene: no @mark moves him, so his hem stays clean.
//     His idle has no breath cycle and his reflection doesn't ripple (Art; sefir_aurane.md).
//   - The barge leaves no wake, and the poles make no water sound: barge_pole is wood and footfalls
//     only. The iron's hiss is the only water sound in the scene.
//   - No close-up on Sefir before his first line: W10 and W11 show him small at the bow.
//   - He must read as kind on a first play: no reaction shot undercuts him. No Liss glare, no Kerrid
//     flinch, no ominous sting, no @vfx. Liss says nothing here; her one line comes in B06, after he
//     has gone. sefir_theme enters only after his first line and resolves on the cut.
//   - Kerrid keeps his back to the barge for the whole scene, for a practical reason (the hull-rib).
//     Sefir's eyes rest on his back for half a beat (@wait 0.5) and move on. Nobody sees it.
//   - The crate: his eyes rest on it a moment too long (@wait 1.5), no line, no change of face.
// The Inquisitor's yield bark ("...Enough. Enough.") opens the scene, on one knee, until a
// battle-bark system can say it at the yield (M3-C06-05).
title: ch06_barge
location: ch06/brine_shoals
---
@letterbox on
// 1. W10, the impasse: the Inquisitor on one knee in the mud, the hound gone.
@camera W10
@music silence
@anim inquisitor kneel
Inquisitor [exhausted]: ...Enough. Enough. #line:ch06_barge_001
@mark stillguard_a impasse_a run via=way_tents_s,way_camp_s
@mark stillguard_b impasse_b run
@anim stillguard_a level_spear
@anim stillguard_b level_spear
@mark toma shield_line walk via=way_tents_e
@anim toma shield_up
@wait 1.5
// 3. Kerrid, before the barge arrives: at the burning hulk, a smouldering hull-rib on his shoulder
//    so two wright children can crawl out from under it. That is why his back is turned.
@mark kerrid hulk_rib walk
@anim kerrid hold_rib_on_shoulder
@anim wright_child_a crawl_out
@anim wright_child_b crawl_out
@wait 1.0
// 2. W11, the barge, from water level: the smoke thins; the stern and the flat water behind it, 3 s.
@camera W11
@sfx barge_pole
@anim reed_a pole_barge
@anim reed_b pole_barge
@anim reed_c pole_barge
@anim reed_d pole_barge
@wait 3.0
@anim stillguard_a kneel_palms_flat
@anim stillguard_b kneel_palms_flat
@anim stillguard_c kneel_palms_flat
@anim wrights look_at sefir
// 4. Back to W10: we see him small at the bow first. The one sentence, to the clerk.
@camera W10
@wait 1.0
Sefir [neutral]: Put the iron in the water, please. #line:ch06_barge_002
@music sefir_theme fade=3.0
@anim clerk iron_into_water
@sfx brine_iron_hiss
@anim stillguard_c let_go brand_girl
@wait 1.0
// 5. The rebuke. He declines the question of who struck his Stillguard.
Inquisitor [worried]: High Warden. They struck the Stillguard. The Cantor's own— #line:ch06_barge_003
Sefir [neutral]: Be level, Inquisitor. The Edict burns things. It has never needed to burn people. #line:ch06_barge_004
Sefir [soft_smile]: The Edict was written by frightened people. We need not be frightened today. #line:ch06_barge_005
@anim sefir look_at wrights
Sefir [tender]: Take them up to Corrow. See that they are fed. #line:ch06_barge_006
// 6. W12, Asha: she bows, palms flat; he bows back, lower than he needs to.
@camera W12
@anim asha bow_palms_flat
@anim sefir bow_from_barge
Sefir [tender]: Lady Cantor. I knelt beside your mother once, on a day very like this one. #line:ch06_barge_007
Asha [neutral]: It would honour me to hear of her, High Warden. #line:ch06_barge_008
Sefir [soft_smile]: And you shall. Come to Ansedra, and we will sit, and I will tell you everything I can. #line:ch06_barge_009
@face asha tender 0.6
@wait 1.0
// 7. Liss and the papers.
Inquisitor [neutral]: And the wright with the crate. #line:ch06_barge_010
@anim sefir look_at asha
Sefir [neutral]: Is she one of yours? #line:ch06_barge_011
Asha [determined]: She's my guardian. #line:ch06_barge_012
@face liss surprised 0.3
@wait 1.0
Sefir [smile]: Then she is. A Cantor may take any guardian she chooses. It is the oldest custom we keep. Toma Okeru, your papers will carry her? #line:ch06_barge_013 #long
Toma [neutral]: ...They will, High Warden. #line:ch06_barge_014
@anim sefir look_at liss
@camera W12_crate
@wait 1.5
@camera W12
// 8. Ysolde.
@anim sefir look_at ysolde
Sefir [neutral]: Scholar Ysel. You will come to the Sanctum this year? #line:ch06_barge_015
Ysolde [neutral]: As every year, High Warden. #line:ch06_barge_016
Sefir [tender]: He will be glad of you. #line:ch06_barge_017
// 9. W13, Sefir's eyeline over the party: it passes Kerrid's back for half a beat and finds Rhen,
//    standing when everyone else is kneeling. He is visibly amused.
@camera W13
@anim sefir look_at kerrid
@wait 0.5
@anim sefir look_at rhen
@wait 0.8
-> Be... still? #line:ch06_barge_018
    Sefir [smile]: That is the answer, young man, not the greeting. But I will take it gladly. #line:ch06_barge_019
    <<set $ch06_rhen_greeted_sefir = true>>
-> Does that barge ever make a wake? #line:ch06_barge_020
    Sefir [soft_smile]: Not if it is poled well. There is very little in the world that needs to hurry. #line:ch06_barge_021
// 10. Toma, last. A cut back to W12's axis: he kneels, palms flat, and his voice goes.
@camera W12
@anim toma kneel_palms_flat
@anim sefir look_at toma
Toma [tender]: Be level, High Warden. #line:ch06_barge_022
Sefir [tender]: And still, Toma Okeru. #line:ch06_barge_023
@face toma tender 0.6
@wait 1.5
// 11. W10, the going. The Reeds pole the barge back into the smoke. Still no wake.
@camera W10
Sefir [soft_smile]: Go gently, Lady Cantor. #line:ch06_barge_024
@sfx barge_pole
@anim reed_a pole_barge
@anim reed_b pole_barge
@anim reed_c pole_barge
@anim reed_d pole_barge
@wait 3.0
<<set $ch06_met_sefir = true>>
@letterbox off
===
